WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.500
In Florida.

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:00.734
Take a

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.368
look at this packed

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.936
event hosted by a bookstore.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.337
It's not a book signing.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.038
People that were there

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.139
last night to support former

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.007
national youth poet

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.074
laureate Amanda Gorman,

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:08.742
who donated

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:10.276
1200 books to be given out,

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.545
including 400 copies of her book

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.546
and two other titles

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.181
restricted at a Miami-Dade

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.950
County public school for kindergarten

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.418
through eighth graders.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.652
The books are being restricted to

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.088
after one parents complaint.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.590
Gorman's book is titled The Hill

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:24.157
We Climb.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.525
It's the same title as the poem

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.326
she read at President

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.293
Biden's inauguration

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.429
in 2021 as the youngest inaugural poet

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.663
in U.S. history.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.132
Months later, her book was published

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.266
and had been available

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.068
at the school library for all students

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.736
until one parents complaint.

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:37.837
And by the way, that parent

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.672
did not actually read the book

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.641
Now, the school district says only middle

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.977
school students have access

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:44.978
to Amanda Gorman's book.

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.613
The parents complaint stated it

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.715
includes, quote, hate messages

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.283
The parent took issue

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.152
with just some lines, Gorman recited.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:53.253
Here are a few of them.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.924
We've braved the belly of the beast.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.092
We've learned

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:01.861
that quiet isn't always peace

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:05.765
in the norms and notions of what just is

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:09.536
isn't always just is.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:13.440
And yet the dawn is hours before

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.340
we knew it.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.775
Somehow we do it.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:18.845
Somehow we've weathered and witnessed

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:22.148
a nation that isn't broken

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.751
but simply unfinished.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.788
And Amanda Gorman joins us now.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.990
And so we're just hearing you do that

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.560
inaugural poem again. It's lovely.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:34.961
It's great to have you back.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.663
And I'm sorry to say, the circumstances

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:39.933
when you've heard this

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.134
What was your initial reaction

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.502
when you found out this,

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.070
that your book is being restricted

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:44.737
by somebody

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:47.740
who had not actually even read it?

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.741
Hmm.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.777
I think my first response

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.779
was this dual experience

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.781
of shock and grief

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:55.748
for the first part,

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.750
because over 40 million people

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:00.220
saw that moment at the inauguration.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.522
And I couldn't imagine a reason

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:03.723
of erasing that

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:04.591
from a bookshelf

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.826
for young readers to see.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.228
And on the flip side,

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.329
I felt this

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.363
anguish and pain

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.965
because so much of the excitement

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.867
that I had while writing The Hill

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.502
We Climb was knowing

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.403
that young people would be able to see

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.005
themselves represented

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.207
in this moment in our democratic history.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.309
And so to have that representation

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.044
taken away from young people

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.880
just felt devastating.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.313
You know,

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:27.914
this is happening

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.949
obviously, in places across the country.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.251
And often it's

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.219
parents who have not read

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.020
any of these books.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:34.521
They often

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:36.623
just get a list of books

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:38.658
from an organization,

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:39.926
a conservative organization

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:42.061
that wants books removed.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.831
And they send that in

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.699
and to show up at a school board meeting

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.134
and the books are taken out.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:50.503
I think you get

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:51.504
absolutely to

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.706
the core of the issue, which is that

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:57.510
you can, in effect, ban restrict

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.612
remove a book like that.

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:00.380
All it takes

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.447
is one person

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:03.016
often who isn't a parent

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.251
or doesn't even need to read that work

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.686
to sign a complaint

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:09.255
and that complaint can be accomplished

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:11.157
pretty quickly, as we saw with

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:12.625
what happened with my book.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:13.426
That form

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.728
can even be filled out inaccurately

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.897
and that can still lead to that

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.733
book being restricted for that school,

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.802
that community, that library.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:23.536
And so what we're

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:25.772
witnessing is a real loophole

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.407
in the educational system

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:29.442
where it's really easy to mobilize

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.878
a small select group of people

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.414
to ban thousands of books over time.

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.182
Now, to get your book,

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:38.651
you've got to go to the media center

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:39.819
and you have to in the school,

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:40.486
you have to prove

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:41.888
that you're at a fifth grade

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:42.922
reading level in order

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.457
to get access to the book.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.992
That's kids

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:46.859
aren't going to discover

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:47.594
a book like that.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:51.097
No, I think you're absolutely correct.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:52.432
And one of the things

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.266
that keeps getting set

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:55.368
around the circumstance of my book

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:56.069
that's been banned

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.804
and other books that were removed

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:58.838
from the elementary school

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.673
shelves at that same school

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.909
due to that same complaint,

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.177
a lot of what gets said

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:05.545
is, oh, it's not banned.

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.513
It's just moves to the elementary side,

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:08.615
to the middle school.

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:09.949
But what you have to keep in

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.651
mind, exactly like what you said,

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:12.885
if a child

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.821
now needs to jump over hurdles

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.689
of going to a different location,

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.591
speaking to a media specialist,

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:19.592
proving themselves

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.995
worthy and ready of reading a book.

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:23.630
Those types of hurdles

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.631
are going to

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:26.432
really impede students

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.668
from having a free, ranging,

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.903
welcoming experience of being able

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.839
to pull a book from a bookshelf

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:33.940
and experience it.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.408
And what you just said

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:39.212
also about the role of parent.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:42.382
I am totally accepting and at peace

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:42.849
with the fact

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:44.217
that not every parent,

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:45.184
not every guardian

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:46.653
is going to like my work.

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:48.388
And I think that's absolutely par

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:49.422
for the course.

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:50.657
But I think the issue is

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:52.659
when one person's dislike

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:53.526
for my work

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.128
leads to everyone else,

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:57.230
not having access to that book.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.398
We're really encroaching

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:00.433
on the rights of families and parents

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.068
and teachers and libraries

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:04.937
to really create access for that

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:05.872
that exist

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:06.773
for other people

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:09.008
who still want that door.

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:09.242
You know,

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.143
there've been a lot of questions

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:12.445
about the motivation behind

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:13.246
a number of these people

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.881
who are doing this in school districts.

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:15.748
Our correspondent

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:17.550
Ellie Reeve, actually went to a mom's

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.318
for Liberty School

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:18.751
Board meeting,

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.753
which is becoming a nationwide group

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:25.591
of of of of people who are behind this

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:27.927
and talked to a leader of a

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:29.228
of a group from Moms for Liberty.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:29.862
I just want to play

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.197
some of what she had to say

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:34.434
To me, it sounds like

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:34.967
you're saying

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.903
there's some kind of high level

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.371
coordinated effort

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:41.741
to make more children trans and good.

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:42.842
Yeah.

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:45.144
Well, who's directing that?

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.714
Teachers unions and

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:48.781
our president

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:51.918
and a lot of funding sources and teachers

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.586
unions are also heavily backing

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:54.320
the curriculum

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.455
that we're bringing into school.

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:57.757
Why would they want more kids

00:05:57.757 --> 00:05:59.158
to be gay and trans?

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:01.060
Because it breaks down the family unit,

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:01.894
which breaks down

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.796
traditional conservative values.

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:05.131
It breaks down a lot of things

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:05.965
in this country

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:06.799
that it changes

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:08.434
the way that people think.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:08.968
It changes

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:11.304
the way that people handle politics.

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:14.674
Which is sort of a fascinating unpeeling

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:15.608
of the onion

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:16.609
that at the core

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:18.678
for this woman in particular,

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:22.382
she believes this is part of a conspiracy

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:26.219
by teacher unions and others to

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:28.421
to destroy conservative values

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:30.757
and destroy the American family.

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:31.891
Does that make any sense to you?

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:34.394
It absolutely makes

00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:35.128
sense to me

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:36.095
and explains

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:38.131
why we've seen such an increase

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:40.600
in spike in book bans over the past

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:41.801
few years.

00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:42.735
For example,

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:46.539
out of the 2500 plus book bans

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:47.473
that we saw

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:49.442
last year, the majority of them,

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:50.543
according to The Washington

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:53.079
Post, came from just 11 people.

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:54.414
And so what we're seeing

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.181
is that

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:57.850
this book, Banning, isn't representative

00:06:58.084 --> 00:06:59.652
of the opinions

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:00.486
and instincts

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:02.822
of most parents, teachers, students,

00:07:03.022 --> 00:07:06.325
but from a really small subset of people

00:07:06.526 --> 00:07:07.393
who believe

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:09.462
that they're protecting children

00:07:09.462 --> 00:07:11.130
from indoctrination.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.532
Of ideas,

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:15.902
of race, of gender, of sexuality.

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:17.170
But at the end of the day,

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:19.005
what they're ultimately doing

00:07:19.005 --> 00:07:22.208
is eradicating the freedom of children

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:25.411
and students from exploring those issues

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:26.479
in a safe

00:07:26.479 --> 00:07:28.648
and protected and educational space

00:07:28.915 --> 00:07:30.249
that can be combined

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:32.285
with the love of learning and reading.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:33.286
You're also partnering

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:34.320
with PEN America to help

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.022
others speak out against book banning.

00:07:37.223 --> 00:07:38.591
How can people help?

00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:40.092
Absolutely.

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:41.761
So if you want to learn more

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:42.562
about book

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:43.863
restrictions and removals

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:45.231
and also how you can have

00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:46.499
your voice heard,

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:49.502
you can visit pen dot org slash action.

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:51.270
We've made a webpage there

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.839
where you can get all the information

00:07:52.839 --> 00:07:54.373
you need about standing up.

00:07:54.373 --> 00:07:56.642
All right. Amanda Gorman, thanks so much.

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:57.176
Thank you.

